    {
      "id": "782b2dbb-5326-46cf-824b-681b728df544",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -224,
        1472
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 896,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## Workflow Overview: Freeform Text to Purchase Order Engine\n\nThis workflow acts as an automated **Procurement Triage Engine** for your purchasing pipeline. It extracts unstructured purchase requests from Gmail, uses AI to parse the required items, and performs fuzzy matching against an Airtable catalog to enforce contract pricing and preferred-vendor rankings. By automating PO generation for matched items and diverting unknown requests to human triage, it ensures rapid, compliant procurement.\n\n\n## Setup Steps\n\n* **Start Workflow** \u2014 Trigger the workflow to check for recent communications.\n* **Fetch Emails** \u2014 Retrieve unread purchase requests and filter out previously processed messages using timestamps.\n* **Format Data** \u2014 Standardize the raw text and extract the requester's contact information.\n* **LLM: Parse Request** \u2014 Transform unstructured text into a structured JSON list containing items, quantities, and urgency flags.\n* **Airtable: Fetch Catalog** \u2014 Load your approved items, standard prices, contract rates, and preferred vendor rankings.\n* **Match & Price Logic** \u2014 Cross-reference requests with the catalog, apply preferred-vendor score bonuses, and enforce contract pricing.\n* **Router: Evaluate Status** \u2014 Split the operational path based on whether the items were successfully matched or require human review.\n* **Create Auto-PO** \u2014 Generate an official approved Purchase Order record directly in the Airtable ERP for fully matched requests.\n* **Sheets: Log Approval** \u2014 Record the transaction details, matched SKUs, and final costs into a centralized audit log."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
